WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.370
Every day, regulated organisations decide who may see what. Qadamar makes

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.740
each of those decisions, explains it, and records it.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:14.033
Each request passes nine checks, always in the same order: from

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:18.227
role, through classification and need-to-know, to context and separation of duty.

00:00:18.227 --> 00:00:22.420
A single deny stops it.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:27.115
Government. Case files carry a classification and compartments. An analyst cleared

00:00:27.115 --> 00:00:30.710
to L two searches the archive: L three files never appear,

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:34.305
not even their titles. And off the trusted network, the reachable

00:00:34.305 --> 00:00:37.900
level drops.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.727
Banking. The officer who creates a payment cannot approve it, or

00:00:43.727 --> 00:00:48.453
release it. Release runs as a certified command, with a single-use,

00:00:48.453 --> 00:00:53.180
signed token. And a document carrying account numbers is never exported.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:58.195
Healthcare. A clinician sees the records of the patients they treat,

00:00:58.195 --> 00:01:02.110
and nothing else. In an emergency, the glass can be broken,

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:06.025
with a reason, for four hours at most. An alert goes

00:01:06.025 --> 00:01:09.940
out, and someone else reviews it.

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.596
Enterprise CRM. A project manager opens a contract: the client, the

00:01:15.596 --> 00:01:20.152
scope, the milestones. The amounts come back masked, because they carry

00:01:20.152 --> 00:01:24.708
the finance class. A finance approver opens the same contract and

00:01:24.708 --> 00:01:29.264
sees them. And if the mask cannot be applied, nothing is

00:01:29.264 --> 00:01:33.820
released.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.620
Every rule change shows its impact first, and needs a second

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:40.320
approver. And every decision lands in a hash-chained log that an

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.020
auditor can verify.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:49.820
Qadamar. Self-hosted access control for regulated organisations.
